# Kademi server JS: GraalJS (.mjs)

This file runs **inside the Kademi platform**, in a sandboxed GraalJS engine. It is not Node.
There is no `require`, no npm, no filesystem, no `java.*`.

Check `APP-INF/controllers.xml`: `.mjs` files load only when the root element declares
`engineVersion="2.0"`. If it declares `1.1` or omits the attribute, this file is never loaded and
the app is on Nashorn `.js` instead.

- **Every platform-invoked function must be on `globalThis`.** A module-scoped `function` is
  invisible to the platform - controller handlers, resolvers, lifecycle callbacks and async task
  functions all fail silently to resolve.
- **`console.*` for logging.** A `log` global exists only to ease migration; do not use it here.
- **Write native modern JavaScript.** `formatter.foreach`, `formatter.eq` and `formatter.isNull`
  are Nashorn compatibility helpers - use `for...of`, `===` and `?.`. Keep `formatter` for dates,
  currency, CSV and building Java collections.
- **`formatter.toJson(obj)`, not `JSON.stringify`, for any Java object** - a Java bean's getters
  are not enumerable, so `JSON.stringify` returns `{}`.
- **No `Java.type`, no `java.*`, no fully-qualified class names** - class filtering blocks them at
  runtime. Use `formatter.newMap()`, `formatter.newArrayList()` or a `services.*` method.
- **Call `securityManager.yield()` inside long loops** or the CPU governor cannot interrupt the
  request.
- **Nothing mutable at module scope.** App instances are shared across accounts; use
  `controllerMappings.cacheBuilder()` with `getCacheValue`, which scopes keys per organisation.

`services`, `formatter`, `controllerMappings`, `views` and `page` are Java objects dispatched
dynamically - nothing checks a method name until that line runs. Confirm any member at
`https://docs.kademi.co/ref/templating/md/<ClassName>.md` before calling it.

Full guidance: the `kademi-server-js` skill, and its `references/graaljs.md`.
